  "answer_text": "**The comic book came first!** Here's a quick breakdown:\n\n- **The Comic:** *The Walking Dead* was a monthly black-and-white American comic that started in **2003**, created and written by Robert Kirkman with artist Tony Moore.\n\n- **The TV Show:** AMC's *The Walking Dead* TV show had a release date of **2010\u20132022**.\n\nSo the comic predates the TV show by **7 years**. AMC's *The Walking Dead* was based on Robert Kirkman's hit comic series, though the show made some huge changes to the source material. For example, fan-favorite character Daryl Dixon doesn't exist in the comics at all, making his existence one of the largest differences between the comics and the TV show.",
